1. Definitions

   "Software" means the source code, binaries, documentation, data, images and other
   material in this repository and in its releases.

   "Research use" means academic or scientific research, experiments, evaluation and
   benchmarking, including inside a company, and publishing results obtained with the
   Software, as long as the Software is not deployed in production or used to provide a
   product or service to others.

   "Non-commercial use" means use that is not intended for, or directed toward,
   commercial advantage or monetary compensation: personal use, teaching and learning,
   and use by non-profit organizations, schools, universities, public research
   institutes and government bodies for their non-commercial purposes.

   "Commercial use" means any use that is neither Research use nor Non-commercial use,
   including using the Software in a business, building it into a product or service,
   or offering its results as a paid service.

   "Annual revenue" means the total gross revenue of an organization together with every
   entity that controls it, is controlled by it, or is under common control with it, in
   its most recently completed fiscal year, in US dollars or the equivalent.

2. Research and non-commercial use — unlimited

   Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person or organization to use,
   copy, modify, merge, publish and distribute the Software and works based on it, for
   Research use and Non-commercial use, without limitation, subject to section 4.

3. Commercial use — free for small organizations

   The permission in section 2 also covers Commercial use by an individual, or by an
   organization whose Annual revenue does not exceed US$1,000,000 (one million US
   dollars), subject to section 4. If an organization's Annual revenue later exceeds that
   amount, this permission for Commercial use ends 90 days after the end of the fiscal
   year in which it was exceeded, unless a separate license has been agreed by then.

